---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const post = {
  title: 'Introducing WhatsApp Business Labels Sync',
  date: 'January 3, 2026',
  readTime: '4 min read',
  category: 'Product Update',
  author: 'WATeamInbox Team',
  description: 'How WATeamInbox brings WhatsApp Business labels and workspace tags into one contact-organization workflow.'
};
---

<Layout
  title={`${post.title} — WATeamInbox Blog`}
  description={post.description}
  type="article"
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-24 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="text-center">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-3">
        <span class="rounded-full bg-primary-100 px-3 py-1 text-sm font-medium text-primary-800">
          {post.category}
        </span>
        <span class="text-gray-500">{post.readTime}</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 md:text-5xl" data-testid="blog-post-title">
        {post.title}
      </h1>
      <div class="mt-6 flex items-center justify-center gap-4 text-gray-600">
        <span>By {post.author}</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <time>{post.date}</time>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Featured Image -->
    <div class="mt-12 flex h-64 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-r from-primary-600 to-primary-800 md:h-96">
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-32 w-32 text-white/60" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M7 7h.01M7 3h5c.512 0 1.024.195 1.414.586l7 7a2 2 0 010 2.828l-7 7a2 2 0 01-2.828 0l-7-7A1.994 1.994 0 013 12V7a4 4 0 014-4z" />
      </svg>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="prose prose-lg mx-auto mt-12 max-w-3xl" data-testid="blog-post-content">
      <p class="lead text-xl text-gray-600">
        WATeamInbox includes a label-sync workflow that connects WhatsApp Business labels with workspace tags. This note explains what the current implementation syncs and where an operator still needs to trigger an action.
      </p>

      <h2>What is Labels Sync?</h2>
      <p>
        WhatsApp Business accounts include labels for organizing contacts and conversations. Labels Sync connects those labels with custom tags in WATeamInbox.
      </p>
      <p>
        This means you can maintain consistent organization across both systems, ensuring your team always has access to the same categorization regardless of which interface they're using.
      </p>

      <h2>Key Features</h2>

      <h3>Sync and apply</h3>
      <p>
        Use "Sync from WhatsApp" to import the labels for a connected account and link them to workspace tags. Applying or removing a linked label from a contact sends that explicit action back to WhatsApp Business; it is not an always-on mirror of every change.
      </p>

      <h3>Auto-Create Tags</h3>
      <p>
        Don't want to manually link each label? Use our "Auto-create Tags" feature to automatically generate custom tags from all your unlinked WhatsApp Business labels with a single click.
      </p>

      <h3>Color Mapping</h3>
      <p>
        WhatsApp Business has 20 predefined label colors. Labels Sync preserves these colors when creating tags, ensuring visual consistency across platforms.
      </p>

      <div class="rounded-lg bg-gray-50 p-6 not-prose my-8">
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">Supported Label Colors</h4>
        <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-5 gap-4">
          <div class="flex flex-col items-center">
            <div class="h-8 w-8 rounded-full bg-[#00a884]"></div>
            <span class="mt-1 text-xs text-gray-500">Green</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex flex-col items-center">
            <div class="h-8 w-8 rounded-full bg-[#53bdeb]"></div>
            <span class="mt-1 text-xs text-gray-500">Blue</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex flex-col items-center">
            <div class="h-8 w-8 rounded-full bg-[#ff9500]"></div>
            <span class="mt-1 text-xs text-gray-500">Orange</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex flex-col items-center">
            <div class="h-8 w-8 rounded-full bg-[#ff2d55]"></div>
            <span class="mt-1 text-xs text-gray-500">Red</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex flex-col items-center">
            <div class="h-8 w-8 rounded-full bg-[#af52de]"></div>
            <span class="mt-1 text-xs text-gray-500">Purple</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>How to Get Started</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Navigate to Settings</strong> - Go to your Settings page and find the "WhatsApp Labels" section.</li>
        <li><strong>Click "Sync from WhatsApp"</strong> - This fetches all your current WhatsApp Business labels.</li>
        <li><strong>Link or Auto-Create</strong> - Either manually link labels to existing tags or use auto-create for quick setup.</li>
        <li><strong>Start Organizing</strong> - Apply labels to contacts and watch them sync in real-time.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>API Access</h2>
      <p>
        For developers, we've exposed a complete REST API for label management:
      </p>

      <div class="rounded-lg bg-gray-900 p-4 not-prose my-6">
        <pre class="text-sm text-gray-100 overflow-x-auto"><code>GET  /api/labels           # List all synced labels
POST /api/labels/sync      # Trigger sync from WhatsApp
POST /api/labels/:id/link  # Link label to a tag
POST /api/labels/auto-create # Auto-create tags from labels</code></pre>
      </div>

      <h2>Current boundary</h2>
      <p>
        Label data can be refreshed, linked, auto-created, applied, and removed through the current settings and API workflow. Treat the WhatsApp account and workspace tags as systems that may diverge until a sync or action completes; do not assume unsupported automation or bulk behavior.
      </p>

      <p>
        Report a reproducible mismatch or missing workflow through the project's <a href="https://github.com/ygncode/wateaminbox/issues">GitHub Issues</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Author Bio -->
    <div class="mt-16 border-t border-gray-200 pt-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
        <div class="flex h-16 w-16 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary-100">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-8 w-8 text-primary-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M16 7a4 4 0 11-8 0 4 4 0 018 0zM12 14a7 7 0 00-7 7h14a7 7 0 00-7-7z" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900">{post.author}</p>
          <p class="text-gray-600">Building the future of business communication.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Related Posts -->
    <div class="mt-16 border-t border-gray-200 pt-8">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Related Articles</h3>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
        <a href="/blog/quick-replies-boost-productivity" class="group rounded-lg border border-gray-200 p-6 transition-shadow hover:shadow-md">
          <span class="text-sm text-cyan-600">Tips & Tricks</span>
          <h4 class="mt-2 font-semibold text-gray-900 group-hover:text-primary-600">How Quick Replies Can Boost Your Team's Productivity</h4>
        </a>
        <a href="/blog/team-collaboration-best-practices" class="group rounded-lg border border-gray-200 p-6 transition-shadow hover:shadow-md">
          <span class="text-sm text-emerald-600">Guide</span>
          <h4 class="mt-2 font-semibold text-gray-900 group-hover:text-primary-600">Team Collaboration Best Practices for WhatsApp Business</h4>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Back to Blog -->
    <div class="mt-12 text-center">
      <a href="/blog" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-700">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
        </svg>
        Back to Blog
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
